    "contentHtml": "\n            <p class=\"lead-text\">Between 2020 and 2022, SaaS companies were valued on pure top-line revenue growth. In 2026, venture capital and public markets reward only one fundamental metric: capital efficiency.</p>\n\n            <p>If your company burns $2.00 to add $1.00 in net-new ARR, your valuation multiple is crushed. The modern benchmark is a <strong>Burn Multiple below 1.0</strong>, achieved through automated revenue engines that decouple pipeline generation from headcount.</p>\n\n            <h2 id=\"the-new-saas-reality\">1. The New SaaS Valuation Reality</h2>\n            <p>Venture debt providers and growth equity investors now scrutinize Magic Number, Rule of 40, and CAC Payback Periods above all else. Adding an army of SDRs and junior media buyers is no longer viable when AI can orchestrate intent-based outbound at a fraction of the cost.</p>\n\n            <h2 id=\"anatomy-of-burn-multiple\">2. Anatomy of the Sub-1.0 Burn Multiple</h2>\n            <p>The Burn Multiple is calculated as <code>Net Burn / Net New ARR</code> over a given period. A score under 1.0 means you generate more recurring revenue than you consume in operating capital.</p>\n\n            <h2 id=\"autonomous-cac-reduction\">3. Slashing CAC Payback to Under 5 Months</h2>\n            <p>How do DSE SaaS partners compress CAC payback from 18 months down to 4.8 months? By eliminating the three biggest revenue leaks:</p>\n            <ol>\n                <li><strong>Wasted Ad Spend:</strong> Real-time exclusion of non-buying accounts and automated budget shift toward high-intent ICP clusters.</li>\n                <li><strong>Lagging Lead Response:</strong> Immediate algorithmic lead qualification and automated personalized briefing documents delivered in under 60 seconds.</li>\n                <li><strong>Content Bottlenecks:</strong> On-demand creation of personalized landing pages and comparison calculators matching the prospect's exact tech stack.</li>\n            </ol>\n        "
