    "contentHtml": "\n            <p class=\"lead-text\">Search has experienced its most profound disruption in 25 years. Today's high-intent enterprise buyers do not click through ten blue links; they ask complex, multi-variable questions to SearchGPT, Perplexity, Claude, and Gemini.</p>\n\n            <p>If your website is not engineered for <strong>Answer Engine Optimization (AEO)</strong>, your brand becomes invisible in the answers delivered to executive buyers.</p>\n\n            <h2 id=\"seo-vs-aeo\">1. The Shift from 10 Blue Links to Synthesized Answers</h2>\n            <p>Traditional SEO focused on keyword stuffing, backlink volume, and superficial page length. In contrast, AI search engines evaluate <em>information gain</em>, consensus authority, and structural extractability. They synthesize answers from the most logically coherent and fact-dense sources available.</p>\n\n            <h2 id=\"information-gain\">2. Information Gain & Fact Density</h2>\n            <p>To be cited by Perplexity or SearchGPT, every heading in your content must provide an unambiguous, direct answer in the first 40 to 60 words, supported by proprietary data, empirical statistics, or unique frameworks that do not exist elsewhere on the web.</p>\n\n            <h2 id=\"knowledge-graph-schema\">3. Schema Knowledge Graph Grounding</h2>\n            <p>LLM search engines rely heavily on Schema.org structured data (such as <code>Organization</code>, <code>Service</code>, <code>TechArticle</code>, and <code>FAQPage</code>) to map your brand's entities, relationships, and service offerings into their knowledge graphs.</p>\n\n            <h2 id=\"citations-measurement\">4. How to Measure & Dominate AI Citations</h2>\n            <p>At DSE AI Solutions, our proprietary Studio platform audits how AI search engines represent your company across competitive queries, engineering citation anchors that ensure your brand is cited as the primary authority.</p>\n        "
